.TH WERKMEISTER-METRICS-REBUILD 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-metrics\-rebuild \- Backfill the metrics event log from record branches, GitHub and transcripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister metrics rebuild\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBWhat it does:\fR
.IP 1. 3
Clones the workspace repo (the origin of \fB<repos_root>/sandbox\-workspace\fR, else \fBoverrides.workspace_repo\fR) into a temporary bare clone, removed when the command ends. The shared checkout is never fetched into or written \" name-check: ignore
.IP 2. 3
On each record branch except the default one: writes \fBstage.done\fR for each stage at the commit that first filled its \fBoutput/\fR, and \fBpr.open\fR / \fBpr.merged\fR at GitHub's \fBcreatedAt\fR / \fBmergedAt\fR for each PR file's \fBurl:\fR (through \fBgh\fR). The ticket comes from the branch's \fBusage.json\fR
.IP 3. 3
Writes \fBask\fR / \fBanswer\fR pairs (AskUserQuestion, ExitPlanMode) from the workspace's Claude Code transcripts still on disk
.IP 4. 3
Appends each new line to \fB~/.werkmeister/metrics/events\-YYYY\-MM.jsonl\fR, the month of the event's own time
.PP
Re\-running adds nothing: a stage, a PR event or a transcript session already in the log is skipped.
.PP
It cannot rebuild \fBqueue.*\fR, \fBgate.*\fR, \fBrelease\fR or wrap\-up asks: nothing on disk holds them.
.PP
\fBWhen to use:\fR
.IP \(bu 3
Once after upgrading to a version with the metrics event log, to cover earlier work
.IP \(bu 3
Before transcripts age out (Claude Code prunes them after about 30 days), to keep their ask/answer times
.PP
The command only appends. Copy \fB~/.werkmeister/metrics\fR first if you want to undo a run.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
